From 77c1538c027570906052fd41b37485d85131aee4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:36:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 37/37] feat(harbor_agent): failure class per rollout; a reply
 cut by the context ends the episode

Every /run response now says why the rollout ended: failure_class (ok,
context_overflow, model_truncation_loop, agent_timeout,
verifier_timeout, infra, other), a short masked failure_detail, and one
0/1 field per class (failure_infra, ...). NeMo-RL logs every numeric
response field per agent, so they reach TensorBoard as
<agent>/failure_<class>/mean without a NeMo-RL change. The server prints
one line per rollout with the class.

The rules (failure_classes.py) read Harbor's exception_info including
the chained causes of its traceback, the verifier phase time, whether
the verifier produced a result, and the agent's agent_error_flags.json.
Harbor's _verify_with_timeout reports every TimeoutError as
VerifierTimeoutError, also the OpenSandbox provider's command-status
timeout (8 of 32 in job 5356101): such a chain, or a verifier timeout
well before its cap, is infra. Terminus2NemoGym catches the exception
that ends its episode so the verifier still runs; it now writes its type
and masked first line to the flags, so a sandbox that died during the
episode (14 rollouts of job 5358015, scored 0 and trained on) is infra
too.

A reply with finish_reason length that is shorter than the output limit,
or whose prompt + reply reach model_info.max_input_tokens (from the
model server's usage numbers), was cut by the context ceiling; a
resample meets the same ceiling (72 of 73 truncation loops in job
5359900). With the new Terminus2NemoGym option context_limit_truncation:
overflow (default) NemoGymLLM raises ContextLengthExceededError, so the
episode ends as a context overflow and the verifier still runs;
resample keeps the old path. The option joins SHARED_AGENT_KWARGS.

The OpenSandbox SDK logs every failed file read at ERROR with the httpx
traceback; a 404 "file not found" (Harbor's best-effort read of
/logs/artifacts, 113 trials of job 5359900) is now one DEBUG line. The
exception still reaches the caller; other read errors keep their ERROR.

Signed-off-by: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
