+### Failure classes
+
+Every `/run` response carries `failure_class` and a short masked `failure_detail` (exception type and
+first line), and one 0/1 field per class: `failure_ok`, `failure_context_overflow`,
+`failure_model_truncation_loop`, `failure_agent_timeout`, `failure_verifier_timeout`, `failure_infra`,
+`failure_other`. NeMo RL logs every numeric response field per agent, so these show up as
+`<agent>/failure_<class>/mean` next to `context_length_exceeded_error`. The server also prints one line per
+rollout: `[harbor_agent] INFO rollout <instance_id> failure_class=<class> reward=<reward> job=<job> detail=...`.
+Rules, first match wins (`failure_classes.py`): `infra` (sandbox start/setup timeouts, sandbox API errors,
+OpenSandbox command-status timeouts also when Harbor reports them as `VerifierTimeoutError`, a
+`VerifierTimeoutError` well before its cap, model-server connection errors, tunnel errors, a Harbor job
+without a result; also when such an error ended the agent's episode and the verifier then ran),
+`agent_timeout`, `verifier_timeout` (ran to its cap), `context_overflow` (the prompt does not fit, at the
+start or later, or a reply was cut by the context ceiling), `model_truncation_loop`
+(`max_consecutive_truncations` replies in a row hit the output limit with room left), `other` (type kept in the
+detail; also no verifier result), else `ok`.
+
+`Terminus2NemoGym` option `context_limit_truncation` (`overflow` by default, or `resample`): a reply with
+`finish_reason: length` that has fewer tokens than the output limit, or whose prompt + reply reach
+`model_info.max_input_tokens` (from the model server's `usage`), was cut by the context ceiling. `overflow`
+ends the episode as a context overflow (like a prompt that does not fit; the verifier still runs);
+`resample` treats it like any other truncation (`truncation_retry`, then the cap).
+
 ### On-policy corrections for multi-turn training
 
 In multi-turn RL training, turn `N+1` is built from the full conversation history
